<title>UK: Australia increases sugar output in 1996 - ISO.</title>
<headline>Australia increases sugar output in 1996 - ISO.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia produced 5.62 million tonnes of sugar in 1996, of which 4.29 million were exported, the International Sugar Organization (ISO) said on Friday.</p>
<p>Australia's sugar production in 1995 amounted to 5.12 million tonnes with exports at 4.59 million, it said.</p>
<p>Canada took the lion's share of the 1996 exports, importing 822,733 tonnes after 652,279 the previous year. It was followed by Korea and Japan, which imported 620,636 and 579,210 tonnes respectively.</p>
<p>Nearly all of the Australian exports were raw sugar, although a very small proportion was white, the ISO said.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
